<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anti-Fascist Council for the National Liberation of Yugoslavia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1942–1945</span> · Also known as AVNOJ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anti-Fascist Council for the National Liberation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> (AVNOJ) was the political assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito">Tito</a>'s Partisan movement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, first convened at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihac">Bihać</a> in November 1942. At its second session at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jajce">Jajce</a> on 29 November 1943 it declared itself the supreme legislative body, barred King Peter II from returning and set out a federal Yugoslavia of equal nations. It became the provisional parliament of Democratic Federal Yugoslavia in 1945.</p></div>
